BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-paye-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=22
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: PAYE and National Insurance payment to HMRC (monthl
 y)
DESCRIPTION:Pay what you owe by the 22nd of the month (or the 19th if payin
 g by post). The amount is the tax and National Insurance reported on your 
 FPS in the previous tax month\, minus any EPS reductions.\nApplies to: Emp
 loyers paying HMRC monthly (other than by cheque through the post)\nNon-wo
 rking-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/running-pa
 yroll/paying-hmrc\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.ht
 ml#united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates
  follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays ar
 e not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-paye-payment-post@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=19
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: PAYE and National Insurance payment to HMRC by post
  (cheque)
DESCRIPTION:If you pay by cheque through the post\, it must reach HMRC by t
 he 19th of the month.\nApplies to: Employers paying HMRC by cheque through
  the post\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.
 gov.uk/pay-paye-tax\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.
 html#united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dat
 es follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays 
 are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-paye-eps@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=19
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Employer Payment Summary (EPS) to claim reductions
DESCRIPTION:In the next tax month (which starts on the 6th)\, you can claim
  any reduction on what you'll owe HMRC (for example statutory pay) by send
 ing an Employer Payment Summary (EPS) by the 19th.\nApplies to: Employers 
 claiming reductions such as statutory pay\nNon-working-day rule: check the
  source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/running-payroll/reporting-to-hmrc\n
 Details: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom\n
 \nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurri
 ng rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sour
 ces last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-p60@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270531
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270601
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=5;BYMONTHDAY=31
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Give employees a P60
DESCRIPTION:Give your employees a P60 by 31 May (for the tax year ending 5 
 April).\nApplies to: Employers running payroll\nNon-working-day rule: chec
 k the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/payroll-annual-reporting\nDeta
 ils: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom\n\nFo
 r information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring r
 ule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources 
 last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-p11d@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270707
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=7;BYMONTHDAY=6
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Report expenses and benefits to HMRC
DESCRIPTION:You must report expenses and benefits to HMRC by 6 July.\nAppli
 es to: Employers that provided taxable expenses and benefits\nNon-working-
 day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/payroll-annual-r
 eporting/report-expenses-and-benefits\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpay
 roll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal 
 or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; week
 ends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-class1a-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270723
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=7;BYMONTHDAY=22
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Class 1A National Insurance payment on benefits
DESCRIPTION:Your Class 1A National Insurance payment must be received by 22
  July (or 19 July if you're paying by post).\nApplies to: Employers that p
 rovided taxable expenses and benefits\nNon-working-day rule: check the sou
 rce.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/payroll-annual-reporting/report-expense
 s-and-benefits\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#
 united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates fo
 llow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are n
 ot applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:de-lohnsteuer-anmeldung-monthly@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=10
SUMMARY:Germany: Lohnsteuer-Anmeldung and payment of withheld wage tax (mon
 thly filers)
DESCRIPTION:The employer must file the Lohnsteuer-Anmeldung and pay the wit
 hheld wage tax to the Betriebsstättenfinanzamt no later than the tenth da
 y after the end of each Lohnsteuer-Anmeldungszeitraum. The period is in pr
 inciple the calendar month.\nApplies to: Employers whose Lohnsteuer-Anmeld
 ungszeitraum is the calendar month (the default)\nNon-working-day rule: ch
 eck the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/estg/__41a.h
 tml\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany\n\n
 For information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring
  rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Source
 s last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:de-lohnsteuer-anmeldung-quarterly@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;BYMONTHDAY=10
SUMMARY:Germany: Lohnsteuer-Anmeldung and payment (quarterly filers)
DESCRIPTION:No later than the tenth day after the end of the calendar quart
 er (the period is the calendar quarter)\, if the wage tax to be remitted f
 or the previous calendar year was more than 1\,080 euros but not more than
  5\,000 euros.\nApplies to: Employers whose prior-year wage tax was over 1
 \,080 and up to 5\,000 euros\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nS
 ource: https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/estg/__41a.html\nDetails: https:
 //www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany\n\nFor information only
 \, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the 
 source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 Oct
 ober 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:de-lohnsteuer-anmeldung-annual@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270111
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=1;BYMONTHDAY=10
SUMMARY:Germany: Lohnsteuer-Anmeldung and payment (annual filers)
DESCRIPTION:No later than the tenth day after the end of the calendar year 
 (the period is the calendar year)\, if the wage tax to be remitted for the
  previous calendar year was not more than 1\,080 euros.\nApplies to: Emplo
 yers whose prior-year wage tax was 1\,080 euros or less\nNon-working-day r
 ule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/estg/
 __41a.html\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germ
 any\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the re
 curring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied.
  Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:de-lohnsteuerbescheinigung@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270301
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=2;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Germany: Electronic Lohnsteuerbescheinigung transmitted to tax auth
 ority
DESCRIPTION:The electronic Lohnsteuerbescheinigung (§ 41b EStG) is transmi
 tted per § 93c AO after the tax period\, by the last day of February of t
 he following year.\nApplies to: Employers closing the Lohnkonto for each e
 mployee\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.ge
 setze-im-internet.de/ao_1977/__93c.html\nDetails: https://www.intelligentp
 ayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany\n\nFor information only\, not legal or ta
 x advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends 
 and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:de-uv-jahresmeldung@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270216
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270217
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=2;BYMONTHDAY=16
SUMMARY:Germany: Special annual report to statutory accident insurance (Jah
 resmeldung zur Unfallversicherung)
DESCRIPTION:For each employee insured in accident insurance in a calendar y
 ear\, the employer must submit a special annual report ("zum 16. Februar d
 es Folgejahres"\, i.e. due 16 February of the following year).\nApplies to
 : Employers with employees insured in statutory accident insurance\nNon-wo
 rking-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gesetze-im-intern
 et.de/sgb_4/__28a.html\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlin
 es.html#germany\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates f
 ollow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are 
 not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#germany
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fr-dsn-under50@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:France: DSN and payment of social contributions (employers under 50
  employees)
DESCRIPTION:Monthly DSN no later than the 15th of the month following the p
 aid work period. Social contributions are due on the 15th of month M+1\, w
 hatever the salary payment date.\nApplies to: Employers with fewer than 50
  employees (average annual headcount at 31 December of the previous year)\
 nNon-working day: If the deadline falls on a public holiday or non-working
  day\, it moves to the next working day. Stated for the DSN filing deadlin
 e\; the payment table does not repeat it.\n\nSource: https://entreprendre.
 service-public.gouv.fr/vosdroits/F34059\nDetails: https://www.intelligentp
 ayroll.eu/deadlines.html#france\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax
  advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends a
 nd holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#france
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fr-dsn-50plus-same-month@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261005
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=5
SUMMARY:France: DSN and payment of social contributions (50+ employees\, pa
 y in same month as work)
DESCRIPTION:Monthly DSN no later than the 5th of the month following the pa
 id work period. For salaries paid in month M\, social contributions are du
 e on the 5th of month M+1.\nApplies to: Employers with 50 employees or mor
 e (payment table is headed "plus de 50") paying salary in the month worked
 \nNon-working day: If the deadline falls on a public holiday or non-workin
 g day\, it moves to the next working day. Stated for the DSN filing deadli
 ne\; the payment table does not repeat it.\n\nSource: https://entreprendre
 .service-public.gouv.fr/vosdroits/F34059\nDetails: https://www.intelligent
 payroll.eu/deadlines.html#france\n\nFor information only\, not legal or ta
 x advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends 
 and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#france
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fr-dsn-50plus-deferred-pay@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:France: Payment of social contributions (50+ employees\, salary pai
 d the month after work)
DESCRIPTION:For salaries paid in month M+1\, social contributions are due o
 n the 15th of month M+1.\nApplies to: Employers with 50+ employees (table 
 says "plus de 50") paying salary in the month after the work period\nNon-w
 orking day: If the deadline falls on a public holiday or non-working day\,
  it moves to the next working day. Stated for the DSN filing deadline\; th
 e payment table does not repeat it.\n\nSource: https://entreprendre.servic
 e-public.gouv.fr/vosdroits/F34059\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll
 .eu/deadlines.html#france\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advic
 e. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and hol
 idays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#france
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fr-cotisations-quarterly-under11@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:France: Quarterly payment of social contributions (option\, under 1
 1 employees)
DESCRIPTION:Employers with fewer than 11 employees that opted for quarterly
  payment pay social contributions on the 15th of the first month of the fo
 llowing quarter.\nApplies to: Employers with fewer than 11 employees that 
 opted for quarterly payment\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSo
 urce: https://entreprendre.service-public.gouv.fr/vosdroits/F34059\nDetail
 s: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#france\n\nFor informat
 ion only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated
  by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last check
 ed 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#france
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-loonaangifte-monthly@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Netherlands: Loonaangifte and payment of loonheffingen (monthly per
 iod)
DESCRIPTION:For monthly aangifte loonheffingen the latest filing and paymen
 t date is the last day of the month after the period (period January 2026:
  28-02-2026\; December 2026: 31-01-2027).\nApplies to: Employers whose aan
 giftetijdvak is a calendar month\nNon-working day: If the date is a Saturd
 ay\, Sunday or public holiday\, payment must arrive before that date.\nSou
 rce for non-working-day rule: https://stichtingenvereniging.belastingdiens
 t.nl/aangifte/aangifte-loonheffingen/loonheffingen-aangeven-en-betalen/\n\
 nSource: https://download.belastingdienst.nl/belastingdienst/docs/tijdvakc
 odes-aangiftedatums-betaaldatums-lh2101t62fd.pdf\nDetails: https://www.int
 elligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#netherlands\n\nFor information only\, no
 t legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the sourc
 e\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 
 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#netherlands
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-loonaangifte-annual@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=1;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Netherlands: Loonaangifte and payment of loonheffingen (annual peri
 od)
DESCRIPTION:For the annual period (tijdvakcode 6400) the latest filing and 
 payment date is 31 January of the following year (31-01-2027 for 2026).\nA
 pplies to: Employers with a year as aangiftetijdvak\nNon-working day: If t
 he date is a Saturday\, Sunday or public holiday\, payment must arrive bef
 ore that date.\nSource for non-working-day rule: https://stichtingenvereni
 ging.belastingdienst.nl/aangifte/aangifte-loonheffingen/loonheffingen-aang
 even-en-betalen/\n\nSource: https://download.belastingdienst.nl/belastingd
 ienst/docs/tijdvakcodes-aangiftedatums-betaaldatums-lh2101t62fd.pdf\nDetai
 ls: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#netherlands\n\nFor in
 formation only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule 
 stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last
  checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#netherlands
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:es-modelo-111-quarterly@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Spain: Modelo 111 quarterly withholding return and payment (IRPF on
  employment income)
DESCRIPTION:Quarterly self-assessment during the first twenty natural days 
 of April\, July\, October and January\, for withholdings of the immediatel
 y preceding natural quarter.\nApplies to: Withholding agents filing Modelo
  111 quarterly (not Grandes empresas or large public administrations)\nNon
 -working day: A deadline that falls on a Saturday or non-working day moves
  to the next working day.\n\nSource: https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es
 /Sede/todas-gestiones/impuestos-tasas/pagos-cuenta/modelo-111-reten_____mo
 niales-imputaciones-renta-autoliquidacion_/instrucciones.html\nDetails: ht
 tps://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain\n\nFor information on
 ly\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by th
 e source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 O
 ctober 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:es-modelo-111-monthly@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=20
SUMMARY:Spain: Modelo 111 monthly withholding return and payment (large com
 panies)
DESCRIPTION:Monthly self-assessment during the first twenty natural days of
  the month following the monthly self-assessment period (Grandes empresas 
 and public administrations with annual budget over 6 million euros).\nAppl
 ies to: Grandes empresas and public administrations with annual budget ove
 r 6 million euros\nNon-working day: A deadline that falls on a Saturday or
  non-working day moves to the next working day.\n\nSource: https://sede.ag
 enciatributaria.gob.es/Sede/todas-gestiones/impuestos-tasas/pagos-cuenta/m
 odelo-111-reten_____moniales-imputaciones-renta-autoliquidacion_/instrucci
 ones.html\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain
 \n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recur
 ring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. So
 urces last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:es-modelo-190@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=1;BYMONTHDAY=31
SUMMARY:Spain: Modelo 190 annual summary of withholdings (IRPF on employmen
 t income)
DESCRIPTION:You must file Modelo 190 if you filed Modelo 111. The period is
 \, in general\, between 1 January and 31 January of the year following the
  one the annual return covers.\nApplies to: Withholding agents that filed 
 Modelo 111\nNon-working day: If the deadline falls on a non-working day\, 
 it ends on the next working day.\n\nSource: https://sede.agenciatributaria
 .gob.es/Sede/irpf/retenciones-ingresos-cuenta-pagos-fraccionados/retencion
 es-ingresos-cuenta/obligaciones-retenedor.html\nDetails: https://www.intel
 ligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain\n\nFor information only\, not legal 
 or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; week
 ends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:es-cotizacion-ss@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=-1
SUMMARY:Spain: Social security contributions payment (Seguridad Social cuot
 as)
DESCRIPTION:Social security contributions are paid within the month followi
 ng the one in which they accrue\, unless the rules of a specific scheme se
 t another period (for example self-employed: within the same month).\nAppl
 ies to: Employers in the general scheme (other schemes may set another per
 iod)\nNon-working day: If the last day is a non-working day\, the deadline
  ends on the previous working day (RD 1415/2004\, art. 8(b)).\n\nSource: h
 ttps://www.boe.es/buscar/act.php?id=BOE-A-2004-11836\nDetails: https://www
 .intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain\n\nFor information only\, not 
 legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\
 ; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 20
 26.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#spain
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:it-ritenute-f24@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=16
SUMMARY:Italy: Payment of withholding tax on employee income (F24)
DESCRIPTION:Withholding agents (sostituti d'imposta) must pay the withholdi
 ngs by the 16th day of the month following the month of payment\, using Fo
 rm F24.\nApplies to: Sostituti d'imposta withholding tax on employee incom
 e\nNon-working day: Payment is on time if made on the first working day af
 ter a deadline that falls on a Saturday or public holiday.\n\nSource: http
 s://www.agenziaentrate.gov.it/portale/schede/pagamenti/f24ritreddlavdip/co
 me-e-quando-si-versa\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines
 .html#italy\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follo
 w the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not 
 applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#italy
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:it-inps-contributi@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261005T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=16
SUMMARY:Italy: Payment of INPS social security contributions
DESCRIPTION:Employers pay social security and welfare contributions by the 
 16th of the month following the month in which the employee performed the 
 work.\nApplies to: Employers of dependent workers\nNon-working-day rule: c
 heck the source.\n\nSource: https://www.inps.it/it/it/inps-comunica/diritt
 i-e-obblighi-in-materia-di-sicurezza-sociale-nell-unione-e/per-le-imprese/
 pagamento-dei-contributi-previdenziali.html\nDetails: https://www.intellig
 entpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#italy\n\nFor information only\, not legal or 
 tax advice. Dates follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekend
 s and holidays are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#italy
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
